sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant PBM as Process Builder Modal
    participant IS as Integration Service
    participant MC as Mailchimp Service
    participant CV as Canva Service
    participant GA as Google Analytics
    participant OAuth as OAuth Provider
    participant API as Backend API

    Note over U, PBM: User configuring process integrations
    PBM->>U: Display integration categories
    PBM->>IS: GET /api/integrations/categories
    IS->>PBM: Return categorized integrations
    PBM->>U: Show "Communication & Email" expanded
    
    Note over U, PBM: Configure existing connections
    U->>PBM: Select Mailchimp checkbox
    PBM->>IS: Check Mailchimp connection status
    IS->>MC: Ping API endpoint
    MC->>IS: Connection healthy
    IS->>PBM: Mailchimp ready (connected)
    PBM->>U: Show green "Connected" badge
    
    U->>PBM: Select Gmail checkbox
    PBM->>IS: Check Gmail connection status
    IS->>IS: Verify OAuth token validity
    IS->>PBM: Gmail ready (connected)
    PBM->>U: Show green "Connected" badge
    
    Note over U, PBM: Configure new integration
    U->>PBM: Expand "Design & Creative" category
    PBM->>U: Show design tools list
    U->>PBM: Select Canva checkbox
    PBM->>IS: Check Canva connection status
    IS->>PBM: Canva not connected
    PBM->>U: Show "Connect Required" status
    
    U->>PBM: Click "Connect Canva"
    PBM->>IS: Initiate Canva OAuth flow
    IS->>OAuth: GET /auth/canva/authorize
    OAuth->>U: Redirect to Canva login
    U->>OAuth: Enter Canva credentials
    OAuth->>U: Show permission consent screen
    U->>OAuth: Grant permissions
    OAuth->>IS: Return authorization code
    IS->>CV: POST /oauth/token (exchange code)
    CV->>IS: Return access token
    IS->>API: Save Canva connection
    API->>IS: Connection saved
    IS->>PBM: Canva connection established
    PBM->>U: Update status to "Connected"
    
    Note over U, PBM: Test integration functionality
    U->>PBM: Click "Configure Selected" button
    PBM->>IS: GET /api/integrations/test-connections
    
    IS->>MC: Test API call (get audiences)
    MC->>IS: Return audience list (success)
    IS->>CV: Test API call (get templates)
    CV->>IS: Return template list (success)
    IS->>GA: Test API call (get properties)
    GA-->>IS: Rate limit exceeded (error)
    
    IS->>PBM: Return test results
    PBM->>U: Show connection test results
    PBM->>U: Display " Mailchimp: Connected"
    PBM->>U: Display " Canva: Connected"
    PBM->>U: Display " Google Analytics: Rate limited"
    
    Note over U, PBM: Handle connection issues
    U->>PBM: Click "Retry Google Analytics"
    PBM->>IS: Retry Google Analytics connection
    IS->>GA: Wait for rate limit reset
    IS->>GA: Retry API call
    GA->>IS: Return analytics data (success)
    IS->>PBM: Google Analytics connection restored
    PBM->>U: Update status to " Connected"
    
    Note over U, PBM: Integration permissions configuration
    U->>PBM: Click "Advanced Configuration"
    PBM->>IS: GET /api/integrations/{id}/permissions
    IS->>PBM: Return available permissions
    PBM->>U: Show permissions interface
    
    U->>PBM: Enable "Read campaigns" for Mailchimp
    U->>PBM: Enable "Create designs" for Canva
    U->>PBM: Enable "Read analytics" for Google Analytics
    PBM->>IS: POST /api/integrations/permissions
    IS->>API: Save permission configuration
    API->>IS: Permissions saved
    IS->>PBM: Configuration updated
    
    Note over PBM: Integration validation
    PBM->>IS: Validate all selected integrations
    IS->>IS: Check connection health
    IS->>IS: Verify permissions scope
    IS->>IS: Test API access levels
    IS->>PBM: All integrations validated
    PBM->>U: Show "3 tools configured successfully"
    
    Note over U, PBM: Save integration configuration
    U->>PBM: Return to process details
    PBM->>API: Save integration preferences
    API->>IS: Store process-integration mapping
    IS->>API: Mapping saved
    API->>PBM: Integration configuration complete
    PBM->>U: Update integration summary "3 tools selected" 